# Force these as binary so git NEVER applies line-ending (CRLF/LF) conversion
# to them, regardless of a contributor's core.autocrlf setting. Git's own
# binary auto-detection usually catches this, but can miss small files that
# are mostly ASCII near the start (e.g. a PDF's header/xref table) — and a
# single \n -> \r\n conversion there shifts byte offsets and corrupts the
# file's internal structure (PDF xref tables, xlsx/docx zip central
# directories, jpg data), which is exactly what happened to the vendor
# reply PDF in this repo.
*.pdf   binary
*.xlsx  binary
*.xls   binary
*.docx  binary
*.doc   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.png   binary
